  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Amplifying Voices and Leadership of LGBT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is aimed at increasing access to funding and accompaniment support for LGBTQI organizations in the three West African Voice project countries, and Liberia (an additional country where OXFAM is also present). Initiative Sankofa d&apos;Afrique de l&apos;Ouest (ISDAO) is proposing to engage in a strategic partnership with Voice to ensure that LGBTQI communities, which are part of the core rightsholder groups of Voice, are not left out. As a LGBTQI activist-led fund in the region, we have a strong background and experiencein grantmaking to LGBTQI-led groups, organizations and networks, through participatory grantmaking. Through this strategic partnership, we propose to utilize our approach, our participatory grantmaking infrastructure, our networks, our staff expertise and experience towards ensuring that LGBTQI-led groups, organizations and networks in Mali, Nigeria, Nigeria and Liberia are able to be more fully engaged in and benefit from Voice&apos;s work in the region.

This proposed collaboration involves the following key components:

1. Co-creation of a call for proposal, implementation of a participatory grantee selection process, provision of technical support in grantee partner management, and implementation of a needs-based capacity strengthening strategy for empowerment grantee partners

2. Award of up to 15 empowerment grants (EUR 5000- EUR 20,000) to rightsholder led LGBTI organisations and collectives in Mali, Niger, Nigeria and Liberia, following a joint call for proposals and participatory grantee selection process coordinated by ISDAO. The selection process would be conducted independently and autonomously by ISDAO, utilizing our existing participatory process. Grants wouldbe awarded and administered by Voice;

3. Implementation of a mindful inclusion capacity strengthening strategy for Oxfam and Voicecountry teams in Liberia, Mali, Niger and Nigeria.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="23">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INITIATIVE SANKOFA D&apos;AFRIQUE DE l&apos;O</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ISDAO is an activist-led fund dedicated to building a West African movement that advocates for sexual diversity and sexual rights through a flexible approach to grantmaking and the strengthening of a culture of philanthropy committed to promoting human rights andsocial justice. Its vision is to contribute to building a just and inclusive West Africa free from violence and discrimination. Itsapproach to delivering its mission is shaped by four pillars: (1) To increase and diversify resources available to support and advance the rights and safety of LGBTQI people, (2) To respond to the realities of the region characterised by a nascent and ever-changing LGBTQI movement and context, (3) Adopt a flexible approach to grantmaking, and (4) To promote advocacyfor change by engaging stakeholders in dialogye and building knowledge. ISDAO is challenging the status quo around resourcing LGBTQI organizing and how activists can be involved in decision-making, as the first activist-led fund dedicated to supporting LGBTQI-led organising in West Africa and the first participatory grantmaker in the sub-region.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
